{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049151 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059757 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059566 :question/math-academy-id "e-4518" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y &=1 \\\\ x-8y-z &=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{a} & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 3 & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{b} & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{c} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n\n\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+4y+0z &=1 \\\\ x-8y-z &=-2 \\\\ 3x+2y-2z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}6 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 3 & 2 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x} = \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}\\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{6} & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -8 & -1 \\\\ 3 & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{2} & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{-2} \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n\n\nTherefore, $a=6,$ $b=2,$ and $c=-2.$"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060276 :question/math-academy-id "q-36181" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-4y+z &=2 \\\\ x-6y+11z &=3 \\\\ 3x-4y-z &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 & a \\\\ 1 & b & c \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 11 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -6 & 11 \\\\ 3 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 3 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,\\,b=-6,\\,c=11.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060277 :question/math-academy-id "q-36184" :question/problem "The system of equations\n$\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x + 6y + 5z &=3 \\\\ x - 4y + 8z &=1 \\\\ - 2y + 8z &=7\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n$\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 6 & a \\\\ 1 & -4 & b \\\\ c & -2 & 8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 7\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nWhat are the values of $a, b$ and $c$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186237776 :question/math-academy-id "q-10004" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y+2z &=0 \\\\ x+2y+3z &=2 \\\\ 3x+y+z &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & a & 2 \\\\ b & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & c\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0x+y+2z &=0 \\\\ x+2y+3z &=2 \\\\ 3x+y+z &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,\\,b=1,\\,c=1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265929 :question/math-academy-id "q-130535" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-5y+z &=1 \\\\ -x-3y+9z &=-2 \\\\ 4x-7y-z &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 & c \\\\ -1 & b & 9 \\\\ a & -7 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 9 \\\\ 4 & -7 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -5 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 9 \\\\ 4 & -7 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=4,\\,b=-3,\\,c=1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265930 :question/math-academy-id "q-130536" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x+y+7z &=5 \\\\ x-4y+8z &=1 \\\\ -6y+9z &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & b \\\\ 0 & a & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}c \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b,$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-3x+y+7z &=5 \\\\ x-4y+8z &=1 \\\\ 0x-6y+9z &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 7 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 8 \\\\ 0 & -6 & 9\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-6,\\,b=8,\\,c=5.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292857 :question/math-academy-id "q-275511" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+2z &=5 \\\\ 2x+6y+5z &=22 \\\\ x-2y-3z &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $1$ | {{field-1}} | $2$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $5$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} | $6$ | $5$ |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | {{field-3}} |  | . |\n|  |  | $1$ | $-2$ | {{field-4}} |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $-1$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+2y+2z &=5 \\\\ 2x+6y+5z &=22 \\\\ x-2y-3z &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 22 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 5 \\\\ 1 & -2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 22 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299537 :question/math-academy-id "q-316961" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-y+z &=0 \\\\ 5x+y-7z &=-2 \\\\ -2x+4y+3z &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $3$ | $-1$ | $1$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | {{field-1}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} | $1$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $-2$ |  | . |\n|  |  | $-2$ | {{field-4}} | $3$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $4$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-y+z &=0 \\\\ 5x+y-7z &=-2 \\\\ -2x+4y+3z &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 5 & 1 & -7 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299540 :question/math-academy-id "q-316977" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+z &=11 \\\\ -x-3y-z &=0 \\\\ 8x+6y+3z &=-9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $1$ | $-1$ | {{field-1}} |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $-1$ | {{field-3}} | $-1$ |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $0$ |  | . |\n|  |  | {{field-4}} | $6$ | $3$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $-9$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+z &=11 \\\\ -x-3y-z &=0 \\\\ 8x+6y+3z &=-9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 8 & 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 8 & 6 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}11 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299541 :question/math-academy-id "q-316983" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+z &=1 \\\\ 3x-y+4z &=8 \\\\ -4x+y+5z &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $1$ | {{field-1}} | $1$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $1$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $3$ | $-1$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $8$ |  | . |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} | $1$ | $5$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+0y+z &=1 \\\\ 3x-y+4z &=8 \\\\ -4x+y+5z &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -1 & 4 \\\\ -4 & 1 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 8 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299542 :question/math-academy-id "q-316985" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-2y+4z &=6 \\\\ y-9z &=-2 \\\\ x-y-8z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $3$ | $-2$ | {{field-1}} |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $6$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $0$ | $1$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $-2$ |  | . |\n|  |  | $1$ | $-1$ | {{field-3}} |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-2y+4z &=6 \\\\ 0x+y-9z &=-2 \\\\ x-y-8z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -9 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -9 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -8\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299543 :question/math-academy-id "q-316987" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7x-4y+6z &=-1 \\\\ -2x+3y &=0 \\\\ x-9y+z &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | $-4$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | {{field-3}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $-2$ | $3$ | $0$ |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $0$ |  | . |\n|  |  | $1$ | {{field-4}} | $1$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $5$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7x-4y+6z &=-1 \\\\ -2x+3y+0z &=0 \\\\ x-9y+z &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -4 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -9 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -4 & 6 \\\\ -2 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -9 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299544 :question/math-academy-id "q-316988" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y &=14 \\\\ 3x+3y+z &=3 \\\\ 5x-8y+4z &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $2$ | $-1$ | {{field-1}} |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $14$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-2}} | $3$ | $1$ |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | {{field-3}} |  | . |\n|  |  | {{field-4}} | $-8$ | $4$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $-7$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+0z &=14 \\\\ 3x+3y+z &=3 \\\\ 5x-8y+4z &=-7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -8 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}14 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 3 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -8 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}14 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -7\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299545 :question/math-academy-id "q-316995" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x &=6 \\\\ 2x+z &=2 \\\\ 3x+4y-2z &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | $0$ | $0$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $6$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $2$ | {{field-2}} | $1$ |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $2$ |  | . |\n|  |  | $3$ | {{field-3}} | $-2$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+0y+0z &=6 \\\\ 2x+0y+z &=2 \\\\ 3x+4y-2z &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299546 :question/math-academy-id "q-316996" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y-z &=1 \\\\ y-3z &=0 \\\\ 4z &=12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $3$ | $2$ | $-1$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $1$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | $1$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $0$ |  | . |\n|  |  | $0$ | {{field-3}} | $4$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y-z &=1 \\\\ 0x+y-3z &=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+4z &=12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186323765 :question/math-academy-id "q-36178" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+2y+8z &=0 \\\\ 2x-5y+4z &=3 \\\\ 5x-4y+7z &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & a \\\\ 2 & b & 4 \\\\ 5 & c & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "We can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 4 \\\\ 5 & -4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=8,\\,b=-5,\\,c=-4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426755 :question/math-academy-id "q-10006" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-z &=0 \\\\ x+y+3z &=2 \\\\ 3x-2y+z &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & b \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ a & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ c \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+0y-z &=0 \\\\ x+y+3z &=2 \\\\ 3x-2y+z &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=3,\\,b=-1,\\,c=2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426758 :question/math-academy-id "q-36179" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+5z &=5 \\\\ -x+5y-3z &=2 \\\\ x-4y+7z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & a & 5 \\\\ b & 5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}c \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+0y+5z &=5 \\\\ -x+5y-3z &=2 \\\\ x-4y+7z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ -1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -4 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=0,\\,b=-1,\\,c=5.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059758 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059567 :question/math-academy-id "e-4519" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z &=4 \\\\ z-x+2 &=-1 \\\\ 2y-2x-4z &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{a} & 1 \\\\ \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{b} & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{c} \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n\nWhat are the values of $a,$ $b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x-y+z &=4 \\\\ -x+0y+z &=-3 \\\\ -2x+2y-4z &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b},$ where\n\n\n\n$$\nA = \\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{b} = \\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x} = \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $A\\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}$ becomes\n\n\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{0} & 1 \\\\ \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{-2} & 2 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ \\bbox[lightgray, 2pt]{-3} \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n\n\nTherefore $a=0,$ $b=-2,$ $c=-3.$"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059953 :question/math-academy-id "q-10000" :question/problem "The system of equations\n$\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2y + 3z &=-1 - x \\\\ 4y &=-5z \\\\ x + 6z - 3 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 4 & b \\\\ 1 & a & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}c \\\\ 0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nWhat are the values of $a, b$ and $c$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186060451 :question/math-academy-id "q-9721" :question/problem "The system of equations\n$\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=6 \\\\ y - x - 2z &=0 \\\\ 3z - 2x - 5 &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$\\begin{bmatrix}a & 0 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & -2 \\\\ -2 & b & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 0 \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}$.\n\nWhat are the values of $a, b$ and $c$?"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265931 :question/math-academy-id "q-130562" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}z-7x-5 &=0 \\\\ 4y-x-3z-2 &=0 \\\\ 2y+x-8 &=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & a \\\\ b & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b,$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-7x+0y+z &=5 \\\\ -x+4y-3z &=2 \\\\ x+2y+0z &=6\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 4 & -3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-3,\\,b=1,\\,c=6.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299547 :question/math-academy-id "q-316998" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2z-2y-5x &=5 \\\\ -3z+3y+4x &=1 \\\\ 2z-2x+y &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $-5$ | {{field-1}} | $2$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $5$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $4$ | $3$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | {{field-3}} |  | . |\n|  |  | $-2$ | {{field-4}} | $2$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $2$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x-2y+2z &=5 \\\\ 4x+3y-3z &=1 \\\\ -2x+y+2z &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -2 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 3 & -3 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299629 :question/math-academy-id "q-317632" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-3y+4 &=7 \\\\ -2x+6z-1 &=8 \\\\ 7y-5z+2 &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $5$ | {{field-1}} | $0$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $-2$ | {{field-3}} | $6$ |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $9$ |  | . |\n|  |  | {{field-4}} | $7$ | $-5$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $-5$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x-3y+0z &=3 \\\\ -2x+0y+6z &=9 \\\\ 0x+7y-5z &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 7 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 9 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186299630 :question/math-academy-id "q-317639" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4z+x-3 &=7 \\\\ 2x-5y+6 &=1 \\\\ 3y+7z-4x+5 &=10\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $1$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $10$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $2$ | {{field-2}} | $0$ |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | {{field-3}} |  | . |\n|  |  | {{field-4}} | $3$ | $7$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $5$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+0y+4z &=10 \\\\ 2x-5y+0z &=-5 \\\\ -4x+3y+7z &=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}10 \\\\ -5 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345090 :question/math-academy-id "q-75490" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2y+5x &=3z+2 \\\\ 3x-6y &=5 \\\\ 2x-3y+5z &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}5 & a & -3 \\\\ 3 & -6 & b \\\\ 2 & c & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5x+2y-3z &=2 \\\\ 3x-6y+0z &=5 \\\\ 2x-3y+5z &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -6 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=2,\\,b=0,\\,c=-3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345093 :question/math-academy-id "q-75500" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2y+3z &=7 \\\\ x+z &=-1 \\\\ 3z-2x+y &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}a & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & b & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0x-2y+3z &=7 \\\\ x+0y+z &=-1 \\\\ -2x+y+3z &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}7 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=0,\\,b=0,\\,c=3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345094 :question/math-academy-id "q-75501" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}5y-3z+x &=2 \\\\ 3z+7x-2y &=5 \\\\ 2x-2y &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}a & 5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & b & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & c\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x+5y-3z &=2 \\\\ 7x-2y+3z &=5 \\\\ 2x-2y+0z &=-1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 7 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & -2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=1,\\,b=-2,\\,c=0.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345096 :question/math-academy-id "q-75506" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-y+z &=1 \\\\ 2z+y+x &=-1 \\\\ 3y-z+x &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}a & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & b \\\\ 1 & c & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}0x-y+z &=1 \\\\ x+y+2z &=-1 \\\\ x+3y-z &=1\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 3 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=0,\\,b=2,\\,c=3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345098 :question/math-academy-id "q-75509" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2y-5x+3z &=-1 \\\\ x-3y &=3 \\\\ -3y+2z-x &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & a & 3 \\\\ 1 & -3 & b \\\\ c & -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x+2y+3z &=-1 \\\\ x-3y+0z &=3 \\\\ -x-3y+2z &=-5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=2,\\,b=0,\\,c=-1.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345099 :question/math-academy-id "q-75511" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+y+z &=-1 \\\\ z+3x-2y &=3 \\\\ -y+2z-x &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & b & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & c\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}a \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2x+y+z &=-1 \\\\ 3x-2y+z &=3 \\\\ -x-y+2z &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-1,\\,b=-2,\\,c=2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345100 :question/math-academy-id "q-75512" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2z+x-5y &=1 \\\\ -y+5z-4x &=-2 \\\\ 2x-6y-z &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & a \\\\ b & -1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & c & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-5y-2z &=1 \\\\ -4x-y+5z &=-2 \\\\ 2x-6y-z &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -6 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -5 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -1 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -6 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-2,\\,b=-4,\\,c=-6.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345101 :question/math-academy-id "q-75513" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}z-5x+2y &=0 \\\\ z &=1-2x \\\\ 7y-3x-2z &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & a & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 7 & c\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ b \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x+2y+z &=0 \\\\ 2x+0y+z &=1 \\\\ -3x+7y-2z &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 7 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=2,\\,b=1,\\,c=-2.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186360768 :question/math-academy-id "q-9720" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}y+2z-x &=1 \\\\ 6y+3x-2z &=2 \\\\ x+3z-y &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}a & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & b & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ c\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nWhat are the values of $a,b$ and $c?$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-x+y+2z &=1 \\\\ 3x+6y-2z &=2 \\\\ x-y+3z &=-3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 6 & -2 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $a=-1,\\,b=6,\\,c=-3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426756 :question/math-academy-id "q-317636" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2z+3x-5 &=4 \\\\ 6z-4y+3 &=15 \\\\ 7y+2x-2 &=11\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | $3$ | $0$ | {{field-1}} |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | {{field-2}} |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | {{field-3}} | $-4$ | $6$ |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | $12$ |  | . |\n|  |  | $2$ | {{field-4}} | $0$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $13$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+0y+2z &=9 \\\\ 0x-4y+6z &=12 \\\\ 2x+7y+0z &=13\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -4 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 7 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 13\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426757 :question/math-academy-id "q-317519" :question/problem "The system of equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}8y+6x-3z+4 &=0 \\\\ 5z-3y+x-6 &=0 \\\\ 7x-4z-y-9 &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | $8$ | $-3$ |  |  |  | $x$ |  |  |  | $-4$ |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | $1$ | $-3$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  | $y$ |  | $=$ |  | {{field-3}} |  | . |\n|  |  | {{field-4}} | $-1$ | $-4$ |  |  |  | $z$ |  |  |  | $9$ |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "First, let's write the system so that $x$, $y$, and $z$ appear in each equation in the correct order and all constants are on the right-hand side of the system:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}6x+8y-3z &=-4 \\\\ x-3y+5z &=6 \\\\ 7x-y-4z &=9\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nNow, we can write the system in the form $Ax=b,$ where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 8 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the coefficient matrix,\n\n$$\nb=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of constants, and\n\n$$\nx=\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis the column vector of variables.\n\nSo, the equation $Ax=b$ becomes\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 8 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 5 \\\\ 7 & -1 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 6 \\\\ 9\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying Entries of a Matrix Product Representing a 3x3 System of Equations by Reorganizing"}] :topic/title "Representing 3x3 Systems of Equations Using a Matrix Product"}
